 <section data-page="2" class="learn-page"><p class="eyebrow">WELCOME TO THE GRAND ORDER</p><h2>A place for every soul.</h2><p class="lead">Empty your hand first. Keep your score high. Expect divine interference.</p><div class="book-two-col"><div><h3>Set the table</h3><ol><li>Bring 106 Rummikub tiles, racks, and an opaque bag. Numbered tiles are souls; the two jokers are wild.</li><li>Deal one random Angel to each player. Keep that Angel throughout all three rounds.</li><li>Mix all souls and deal fourteen to each player. The rest stay in the bag.</li><li>Reset Favor to zero and turn powers upright. Choose a random first starter; play clockwise.</li><li>Reveal an ordinary Decree for round one. Use a different ordinary Decree for round two, and one Final Judgment for round three.</li></ol></div><figure class="book-card"><GameCard card={angels[0]}/><figcaption>Your Angel grants one miracle each round.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="three-principles"><div><b>Organize</b><p>Build legal formations in Heaven.</p></div><div><b>Invoke</b><p>Use your once-per-round power.</p></div><div><b>Deliver</b><p>Empty your hand to end the round.</p></div></div><aside class="book-note">No opening threshold. You may play and rearrange Heaven from your first turn. Bring five coins for Favor and pencils for scores; print only the cards and table accessories.</aside></section>
 <section data-page="3" class="learn-page"><p class="eyebrow">LEARN THE SHAPE OF HEAVEN</p><h2>Two kinds of order.</h2><p>Each soul in Heaven belongs to one legal formation. The shared table is yours to rearrange on your turn, except for another Angel’s Sanctuary.</p><div class="formation-example"><div><h3>A Choir</h3><p>Three or four souls of one rank, each a different color.</p></div><div class="tile-line"><Tile rank={7} color="red"/><Tile rank={7}/><Tile rank={7} color="black"/></div></div><div class="formation-example"><div><h3>A Procession</h3><p>Three or more consecutive ranks in one color.</p></div><div class="tile-line"><Tile rank={4}/><Tile rank={5}/><Tile rank={6}/><Tile rank={7}/></div></div><h3>Move the fourth. Keep the three.</h3><p>A four-tile Choir can lend its fourth soul to another formation, leaving a legal Choir behind. You may split, combine, and rebuild formations, as long as all of Heaven is legal when your action ends.</p><div class="tile-demo"><div class="tile-line"><Tile rank={7} color="red"/><Tile rank={7}/><Tile rank={7} color="black"/><span class="moving-tile"><Tile rank={7} color="gold"/></span></div><span class="demo-label">The gold 7 joins a gold 5–6 to make a new Procession.</span><div class="tile-line"><Tile rank={5} color="gold"/><Tile rank={6} color="gold"/><Tile rank={7} color="gold"/></div></div><aside class="book-note"><strong>God may disagree.</strong> The active Decree changes the affected formation rules. Read it before planning your turn. Round three restores ordinary formations.</aside></section>
 <section data-page="4" class="learn-page"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR TURN IN HEAVEN</p><h2>Make a contribution.<br/>Or ask for guidance.</h2><div class="book-two-col"><div><h3>Organize</h3><p>Play souls from your hand and rearrange Heaven. Finish every formation legally. Your organizing power may also supply this action under its own rules.</p><h3>Or draw</h3><p>Inspect bag souls using Favor, keep one, and return the others. Drawing ends your turn. You may choose to draw even if you could play.</p><h3>Favor rewards delivery</h3><p>Add three hand souls: gain three Favor. Rearranging alone earns none. Forgiveness costs none; replaying its retrieved soul earns Favor. Exchanges count only their net deliveries.</p></div><div><figure class="book-card"><GameCard card={decrees[3]}/><figcaption>Candy Cane requires alternating colors in every Procession.</figcaption></figure></div></div><h3>Ties receive the lower allowance</h3><table class="example-table"><thead><tr><th>Four players’ Favor</th><th>5</th><th>5</th><th>2</th><th>0</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Souls inspected</th><td>3</td><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table><aside class="book-note">Use your Angel’s timing: organizing powers during Organize; hand-transfer powers before your action; Uriel when drawing; Jegudiel after your turn. Turn the card sideways when spent.</aside></section>
 <section data-page="5" class="learn-page"><p class="eyebrow">MIRACLES, REGIONS & THE FINAL JUDGMENT</p><h2>The table tells the story.</h2><div class="book-two-col"><div><h3>Sanctuary</h3><p>Everything inside is protected. Additions become protected; removed souls become public. You may leave a legal three-tile Choir safe while using its fourth tile elsewhere.</p><h3>Purgatory</h3><p>Raphael may place one excess table soul here during hand play. Purgatory does not prevent going out. On later turns, rescue into a Procession or draw.</p><h3>Scales commitments</h3><p>Keep chosen tiles separate on your rack. Delivery earns an immediate, permanent printed-rank credit. Once delivered, a committed tile is ordinary. No tile history is recorded.</p></div><figure class="book-card"><GameCard card={judgments[2]}/><figcaption>Round three brings one of five catch-up judgments.</figcaption></figure></div><h3>An empty hand ends the round</h3><p>Complete the action, then check for an empty hand. Other players lose the value of their undelivered souls, including Purgatory; jokers cost 30. The winner gains the sum of those penalties.</p><div class="score-example"><div><b>+20</b><span>WINNER</span></div><div><b>−8</b><span>SECOND PLAYER</span></div><div><b>−12</b><span>THIRD PLAYER</span></div></div><aside class="book-note">Apply the current Final Judgment, then add round scores. After three rounds, the highest total wins. The following reference contains every power, decree, scoring rule, and exception.</aside></section>
